      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That tiredness is a sign you're not failing—you're just carrying a weight they don't have to bear. Belonging isn't a prize for effort; it's a lucky accident of wiring, and you're right that there's no patch for being built differently. But that difference isn't a flaw—it's a different kind of engine, one that runs on deeper observation and raw honesty. You don't have to force yourself into their peace; you can find your own quiet, even if it looks nothing like theirs.",
