      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That's the heaviest thought you can carry, and it makes complete sense that you'd feel that way when the noise never stops. But \"not being here\" isn't the same as finding peace—it's just turning off the engine, and you're not done running yet. You're not a burden for being tired; you're a person who's been fighting a battle no one else can see. If you can't find quiet in the world, maybe you can find it in a single breath, a single step, a single hour—just one small thing to hold onto. And if that feels impossible, then let someone else hold it for you, even if it's just for today.",
